  body: "# Part-week payment and its local notional-entitlement meaning\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\
    \nFor its part-week provisions, the source defines notional entitlement through different JSA(Cont)
    and JSA(IB)/IS amounts and distinguishes the relevant week; it also retains a JSA(Cont) share-fisherman
    exception.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nNotional entitlement here is a local payment concept, not
    notional income or capital. DMG 33103 requires a whole week for the specified JSA(Cont) share-fisherman
    case while retaining ordinary part-week treatment for JSA(IB)/IS. No fraction, current rate or award
    is calculated.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 33100, PDF page 13](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67349b9c0b168c11ea823019/dmgch33.pdf#page=13)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 33: Payment questions.\n- [DMG 33101, PDF page 13](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67349b9c0b168c11ea823019/dmgch33.pdf#page=13)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 33: Payment questions.\n- [DMG 33102, PDF page 13](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67349b9c0b168c11ea823019/dmgch33.pdf#page=13)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 33: Payment questions.\n- [DMG 33103, PDF page 14](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67349b9c0b168c11ea823019/dmgch33.pdf#page=14)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 33: Payment questions.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol6-ch33`: PDF SHA-256 `8dfef5032a37a357a10503574a00872e4af713b89d2c83463e8ee948b33c38c1`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `f62f3e307149fe6c547a171b9c4be4ec49d0b49855ba6ab87630c29ba132f3b7`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsa-personal-rate
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The local notional-entitlement definition uses the JSA(Cont) personal rate,
      separately from the income-based and IS amounts.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch33/0013
      quote: "33101 In this guidance notional entitlement means\n\n\n1. in JSA(Cont), the claimant's personal
        rate\n\n\n2. in JSA(IB) and IS, the amount by which the applicable amount exceeds income.\n\n\n\
        \n\nWhat is the relevant week - JSA and IS"
      locator: DMG 33101
  - target: term/jsais-share-fisherman
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The part-week passage expressly distinguishes JSA(Cont) share fishermen from
      JSA(IB)/IS rather than treating every share fisherman identically.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch33/0014
      quote: "33103 Most JSA and IS claimants including JSA joint-claim couples will be able to get part-week\n\
        payments. But share fishermen will receive payments of JSA(Cont) for whole weeks only. If they
        claim\nJSA(IB) or IS normal part-week payment rules apply. Guidance on share fishermen is in DMG
        Chapter 27."
      locator: DMG 33103
